of a possible T7-8-9 Chow. If I get T7, I can form that. \n\nBut the player across has played T9, so maybe they have T7 or T8. \n\nHmm. \n\nConsidering all this, the best move might be to play F2. It's a Wind tile, but since I have only one and it's my Seat Wind, but I can't form a Pung. Discarding it would not help others much. \n\nSo the answer is Play F2.\n", "output": "Evaluation: [The best move is to discard F2 (South Wind) as it is less likely to be useful for others' melds and maintains potential for future strategies.]\nReason: [Discarding F2 minimizes the risk of aiding opponents in completing their melds. South Wind is the player's Seat Wind, but with only one in hand, it cannot form a Pung or Kong. Keeping terminals (W8, W9) and suited tiles (T1, T2, T4) preserves flexibility for future Chows or sequences.]\nAnswer: Play F2"}
